<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources>

    <!-- Plain app theme — used AFTER the splash hands off. -->
    <style name="Theme.WarattilV2" parent="android:Theme.Material.Light.NoActionBar" />

    <!--
      Starting theme — applied to the launcher Activity. The SplashScreen
      API (API 31+, backported via core-splashscreen on older devices)
      paints this while the app process boots, BEFORE Compose can render
      its first frame.

      DELIBERATELY INVISIBLE ICON (2026-04-22 round 6):
      The Android SplashScreen API has NO official "no icon" mode. If
      `windowSplashScreenAnimatedIcon` is OMITTED, the platform falls
      back to the launcher icon with its default adaptive-icon treatment
      (white disc bubble + shrunken foreground). Nasser saw the fallback
      and reported it as yet another "old intro" — he wants the
      cold-start canvas to be visually empty, not branded with a
      mini-logo.

      Fix: point the splash at a deliberately invisible drawable
      (splash_icon_invisible.xml — a solid-cream 288dp vector) AND
      pin the icon-background bubble to the same cream color. Result:
      the splash renders a cream square masked to a cream circle on a
      cream screen = invisible to the user.

      History:
        Round 5 (just omit the icon)      → fell back to launcher icon
        Round 6 (this): explicit invisible → no visible splash content

      Rationale for two-stage design: the system splash is MANDATORY on
      Android 12+ (shown by the OS during process startup, before any
      app code runs). It can only render a background + icon — it can
      NOT render the Muzzammil ayah block. So we accept it as an
      unavoidable cold-start bridge and make it look like nothing, and
      put the full branded trademark (logo + ayah + attribution) into
      Stage 2 (Compose WarattilSplashScreen), which takes over the
      moment Compose's first frame paints.

      Duration is controlled in MainActivity (SPLASH_MIN_MS = 4000 ms
      on Stage 2; Stage 1 dismisses the instant Compose's first frame
      paints).
    -->
    <style name="Theme.App.Starting" parent="Theme.SplashScreen">
        <item name="windowSplashScreenBackground">#F5F5DC</item>
        <item name="windowSplashScreenAnimatedIcon">@drawable/splash_icon_invisible</item>
        <item name="windowSplashScreenIconBackgroundColor">#F5F5DC</item>
        <item name="postSplashScreenTheme">@style/Theme.WarattilV2</item>
    </style>

</resources>
